cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or cite KSODI v3.51, please cite this fixed public release."
title: "KSODI v3.51: Public Research Repository"
version: "3.51"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24196705"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
authors:
  - family-names: "Steinacker-Folkerts"
    given-names: "Anne"
  - family-names: "Folkerts"
    given-names: "Heiko"
abstract: >-
  KSODI (Kontextsensitive Semantische Operatoren fuer Digitale Interaktion) is
  a structured, non-normative observation method for interaction dynamics in
  human-AI and multi-agent settings. The fixed public v3.51 repository snapshot
  includes KSODI-Light; the complete monadic Standard-Eval line with the five
  operator families, complete typed Z and the IK view family; and the current
  KSODI-Full Layer-4 R_0 gate and Layer-5 dyadic IK_rel projection. Reproducible
  synthetic reference packages accompany Layers 3 to 5. Independent runtime
  conformance, empirical calibration and later R-family layers remain open.
keywords:
  - interaction dynamics
  - human-AI interaction
  - multi-agent systems
  - observability
  - AI governance
  - communication theory
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alkiri-dAraion/KSODI-Public"
url: "https://github.com/Alkiri-dAraion/KSODI-Public"
